{#- ==========================================================================
    STDENV for the {{ stc_name }} started task.

    BPXBATCH reads this file literally: one NAME=VALUE per record, starting in
    column 1. There is no export keyword, no $VAR expansion, no quoting and no
    comment syntax, and trailing blanks are kept. That is why these notes are a
    Jinja comment: nothing here reaches the file. Every value is fully
    resolved from inputs.yml.

    This file is the only place the worker's environment is set. The start
    script sets nothing, so nothing overrides anything. (The guide set
    KAFKA_OPTS here and again in the start script, and one of them was lost.)

    - Heap goes in KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS. connect-distributed.sh only defaults it
      (-Xms256M -Xmx2G) when unset.
    - KAFKA_JVM_PERFORMANCE_OPTS is set because kafka-run-class.sh otherwise
      injects HotSpot G1 flags, which IBM Semeru (OpenJ9) silently ignores.
      gencon is OpenJ9's default policy; stating it makes the choice visible.
      zIIP eligibility (-Xifa) is on by default and must stay on.
    - No CLASSPATH: the MQ jars are symlinked into each connector's lib/
      (Confluent: "do not export the CLASSPATH").
    - LIBPATH carries the MQ bindings native library directory. On z/OS it
      is <mq>/java/lib for both 31- and 64-bit.
    ========================================================================== -#}
JAVA_HOME={{ zos_java_home }}
PATH={{ zos_bash_path | dirname }}:{{ zos_java_home }}/bin:/bin:/usr/bin
LIBPATH=/lib:/usr/lib:{{ mq_install_path }}/java/lib
KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=-Xms{{ connect_heap }} -Xmx{{ connect_heap }}
KAFKA_JVM_PERFORMANCE_OPTS=-Xgcpolicy:gencon -Djava.awt.headless=true
{% if racf_keyring_enabled | bool %}
KAFKA_OPTS=-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore=safkeyringjce://{{ stc_user | upper }}/{{ racf_keyring }} -Djavax.net.ssl.trustStoreType=JCERACFKS
{% endif %}
KAFKA_LOG4J_OPTS=-Dlog4j2.configurationFile={{ connect_config_dir }}/connect-log4j2.yaml
LOG_DIR={{ connect_logs_dir }}
_BPXK_AUTOCVT=ON
